{"book":24,"chapter":43,"context":{"chapter":43,"title":"Into Egypt","summary":"The leaders call Jeremiah a liar, blame Baruch, and take the whole remnant, including Jeremiah and Baruch, to Tahpanhes in Egypt. There Jeremiah buries large stones at the entrance of Pharaoh's building and announces that Nebuchadnezzar will set his throne on that very spot and strike Egypt.","background":"Tahpanhes was a frontier fortress city in the eastern Nile Delta, on the road from Judah. A fragmentary Babylonian text records a campaign by Nebuchadnezzar against Egypt around 568 BC. 'Beth-shemesh' (v. 13), 'house of the sun,' is the Egyptian city Heliopolis, famous for its obelisks.","customs":[{"term":"The clay in the brickkiln","verses":"43:9","note":"The Hebrew may mean a brick pavement or terrace at the building's entrance. The stones were hidden in its mortar as a marker for the coming throne."}],"watchFor":["The accusation against Baruch (v. 3).","'They obeyed not the voice of the Lord' (vv. 4, 7).","Nebuchadnezzar is again called 'my servant' (v. 10)."],"connections":["Jeremiah 46:13-14","Ezekiel 29:19","Deuteronomy 28:68","Jeremiah 2:16"]},"verses":{"1":{"w":[["וַיְהִי","vayhi","H1961","Hc/Vqw3ms","and it was"],["כְּכַלּוֹת","kekhalot","H3615","HR/Vpcc","when had finished"],["יִרְמְיָהוּ","yirmeyahu","H3414","HNpm","Jeremiah"],["לְדַבֵּר","ledaber","H1696","HR/Vpcc","to speak"],["אֶל","'el-","H413","HR","to"],["כָּל","kol-","H3605","HNcmsc","all"],["הָעָם","ha'am","H5971","HTd/Ncmsa","the people"],["אֶת","'et-","H853","HTo","<obj.>"],["כָּל","kol-","H3605","HNcmsc","all"],["דִּבְרֵי","divrei","H1697","HNcmpc","[the] words of"],["יְהוָה","yahweh","H3068","HNpt","Yahweh"],["אֱלֹהֵיהֶם","'eloheihem","H430","HNcmpc/Sp3mp","God their"],["אֲשֶׁר","'asher","H834","HTr","which"],["שְׁלָחוֹ","shelacho","H7971","HVqp3ms/Sp3ms","he had sent him"],["יְהוָה","yahweh","H3068","HNpt","Yahweh"],["אֱלֹהֵיהֶם","'eloheihem","H430","HNcmpc/Sp3mp","God their"],["אֲלֵיהֶם","'aleihem","H413","HRd